From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 23:13:25 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: mediatek: btcvsd: leave loopback to idle when no stream
 is open

Writing 0 to the loopback switch moves both streams to running, even
when loopback was off and nothing is open, as alsactl restore would. That
opens the gate and enables the interrupt with no stream behind it, and it
stays open.

Act only when leaving loopback, and return each direction to running only
if it has a stream.
---
 sound/soc/mediatek/common/mtk-btcvsd.c | 9 ++++++---
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/mediatek/common/mtk-btcvsd.c b/sound/soc/mediatek/common/mtk-btcvsd.c
index 6c5a903cf..8d54c639a 100644
--- a/sound/soc/mediatek/common/mtk-btcvsd.c
+++ b/sound/soc/mediatek/common/mtk-btcvsd.c
@@ -1095,9 +1095,12 @@ static int btcvsd_loopback_set(struct snd_kcontrol *kcontrol,
 	if (ucontrol->value.integer.value[0]) {
 		mtk_btcvsd_snd_set_state(bt, bt->tx, BT_SCO_STATE_LOOPBACK);
 		mtk_btcvsd_snd_set_state(bt, bt->rx, BT_SCO_STATE_LOOPBACK);
-	} else {
-		mtk_btcvsd_snd_set_state(bt, bt->tx, BT_SCO_STATE_RUNNING);
-		mtk_btcvsd_snd_set_state(bt, bt->rx, BT_SCO_STATE_RUNNING);
+	} else if (bt->tx->state == BT_SCO_STATE_LOOPBACK) {
+		/* A stream with nobody behind it would open the gate for good. */
+		mtk_btcvsd_snd_set_state(bt, bt->tx, bt->tx->substream ?
+					 BT_SCO_STATE_RUNNING : BT_SCO_STATE_IDLE);
+		mtk_btcvsd_snd_set_state(bt, bt->rx, bt->rx->substream ?
+					 BT_SCO_STATE_RUNNING : BT_SCO_STATE_IDLE);
 	}
 	return 0;
 }
